@startuml
' As-built detail + trust-report + submission flow.
' The review model is gone (V21__drop_reviews.sql drops shelter_reviews and
' review_reports): there is no review list, no review write/delete and no
' star rating anywhere in the app. The file name is historical (the build
' pack lists this diagram by name); the surviving flows are below.
title Shelter Detail, Trust Reports & Submission Flow (M5-M6, M8, M11)

actor Person

participant "ShelterDetailPage" as DP
participant "SubmitShelterPage" as SP
participant "ContributionsPanel" as CP
participant "ShelterGateway" as SHG
participant "GeoGateway" as GG
participant "GeocodeGateway" as GCG
participant "OSM Nominatim (external, client-side)" as NOM
participant "ApiClient" as AC
database "Spring Boot API" as API

== Shelter detail (public) ==
Person -> DP : open /shelters/123
DP -> SHG : get(123)
SHG -> AC : get<ShelterDetailDto>('/api/shelters/123')
AC -> API : GET /api/shelters/123
API --> AC : ShelterDetailDto (the list fields + yourOccupancyBand + yourOpenStatus)
note over DP
  The detail read is public for ALL statuses (incl. auto-hidden / rejected).
  Header badges come from the shared copy, only when the DTO carries the
  state (never client-derived): the provenance chip (provenance), the
  "Reported (n)" badge (nonexistentReports > 0), the open/closed text
  (openStatus) and the occupancy text (occupancy - firm or hedged band).
end note
note over DP
  Location section: a static Leaflet map (page-scoped LeafletService,
  the same service as /map) flown to the shelter (SHELTER_ZOOM 16) with
  one non-interactive marker. The header also carries the navigate deep
  links (Google Maps walking / Apple Maps, target=_blank rel=noopener)
  and the "Distance from you" action (client-side Haversine - no backend
  call, no IP geolocation).
end note
DP --> Person : shelter info + location map + navigate/distance actions

== Report this shelter (verified viewers) ==
note over DP
  Verified only: anonymous / unverified get the login/verify prompts.
  The picker offers NON_EXISTENT, WRONG_LOCATION and OTHER (the factual
  types carry a detail field, <= 500 chars); CLOSED / OPEN_CONFIRMED stay
  in the ShelterReportType union for stored rows but are no longer picker
  options - open/closed has its own live picker below. One report per
  (shelter, user, type); the duplicate check (409) runs BEFORE the shared
  per-user throttle budget (10 report-type actions / rolling hour -> 429).
end note
Person -> DP : "Report" -> pick a type + detail (factual types only)
DP -> SHG : report(123, {type, detail?})
SHG -> AC : post<ShelterReportResult>('/api/shelters/123/reports', body)
AC -> API : POST /api/shelters/123/reports
alt 200 {damped: true|false}
  DP -> SHG : get(123)   ' the trust badges may have changed
  DP --> Person : picker closed + success notice (damped copy when true) + refetched shelter
else 409 duplicate (shelter, user, type)
  API --> AC : ErrorResponse 409
  DP --> Person : the server's message inline near the picker
else 403 (unverified) / 429 (throttle)
  API --> AC : ErrorResponse
  DP --> Person : banner (verify prompt / "slow down" copy)
end

== Report how full (verified viewers) ==
note over DP
  Three large band buttons (Space available / Getting full / Full) -
  one tap, latest-wins upsert (NO 409: a re-tap is the update).
  Pre-selected from the detail DTO's yourOccupancyBand. Display-only
  server-side: 2 h freshness, latest fresh band wins, 1 agreeing report
  = hedged copy ("Reported full"), 2+ = firm ("Full").
end note
Person -> DP : tap a band button
DP -> SHG : reportOccupancy(123, band)
SHG -> AC : put<void>('/api/shelters/123/occupancy', {band})
AC -> API : PUT /api/shelters/123/occupancy
alt 204 No Content
  DP -> SHG : get(123)
  DP --> Person : the aggregate + recency line updated (occupancyText)
else 403 (unverified) / 429 (throttle)
  API --> AC : ErrorResponse
  DP --> Person : banner
end

== Report open / closed (verified viewers) ==
note over DP
  Two state buttons (Open / Closed) - one live state per user per
  shelter, latest edit wins (NO 409: a re-tap is the update). Pre-selected
  from the detail DTO's yourOpenStatus. NOT throttled - a tap is a state,
  not a report action (it consumes no action-log budget). Display-only
  server-side: 2 h freshness, the latest fresh state wins, 1 agreeing
  report = hedged copy ("Reported closed"), 2+ = firm ("Closed").
end note
Person -> DP : tap Open or Closed
DP -> SHG : putOpenStatus(123, state)
SHG -> AC : put<void>('/api/shelters/123/open-status', {state})
AC -> API : PUT /api/shelters/123/open-status
alt 204 No Content
  DP -> SHG : get(123)
  DP --> Person : the status row + badges updated (openStatus)
else 400 (bad enum) / 403 (unverified) / 404
  API --> AC : ErrorResponse
  DP --> Person : banner
end

== Submit a shelter (verified users) ==
note over SP
  Route /submit guarded by AuthGuard + VerifiedGuard. The location
  section keeps ONE shared location signal written by FIVE capture
  modes: (1) smart text input - coordinate strings (incl. DMS, auto
  lng/lat swap), long-form map URLs parsed client-side by the pure
  parseLocationInput (shared/location-input.ts); (2) "Use my location"
  geolocation; (3) mini-map click/drag; (4) maps.app.goo.gl short links
  resolved by the backend (POST /api/geo/resolve); (5) Estonia address
  search - client-side Nominatim geocoding via GeocodeGateway (one
  deliberate request per press, hard 1 req/s spacing, always-rendered
  "(c) OpenStreetMap contributors" attribution). The read-only
  coordinate readout (+ source/swapped/accuracy hints) is a DISPLAY of
  the shared signal, not a capture mode. A FAILED capture clears the pin
  (never a silent stale pin) - a failed address SEARCH never touches the
  pin (inline state only, never blocks submit). The page pre-checks the
  Estonia bbox client-side (inline error, nothing is sent) and the
  backend re-checks (400 otherwise). capacity 1..100_000,
  description <= 2000 chars.
end note
Person -> SP : fill name, description, capacity
group capture the location (any order, repeats allowed)
  alt typed coordinates / DMS / long-form map URL
    Person -> SP : type text + Enter (or "Set location")
    SP --> Person : shared location set - marker + read-only readout
    note right of SP
      parseLocationInput: bbox gate, (lng,lat) auto-swap,
      inline error on no-pair / out-of-bounds / invalid
    end note
  else "Use my location"
    Person -> SP : click geolocation
    SP --> Person : marker at device position + accuracy hint
  else mini-map pick
    Person -> SP : click / drag the pin
    SP --> Person : shared location set (marker follows)
  else maps.app.goo.gl short link
    Person -> SP : paste short link + "Set location"
    SP -> GG : resolve(url)   ' "Resolving..." pending state
    GG -> AC : post<LocationResolved>('/api/geo/resolve', {url})
    AC -> API : POST /api/geo/resolve
    alt 200
      API --> AC : LocationResolved {latitude, longitude}
      SP --> Person : shared location set (same as a pick)
    else 400 / 429 / 502
      API --> AC : ErrorResponse
      SP --> Person : inline error (pin cleared; 429 = "try again in a minute")
    end
  else Estonia address search (client-side Nominatim)
    Person -> SP : type address + "Search" (or Enter)   ' no autosuggest
    SP -> GCG : search(query)   ' "Searching..." pending; hard 1 req/s spacing
    GCG -> NOM : GET /search?format=jsonv2&limit=5&countrycodes=ee
    NOM --> GCG : <= 5 results (display name + string lat/lon)
    GCG --> SP : results (429 -> "please wait a moment"; network -> generic copy)
    Person -> SP : pick a result
    SP --> Person : shared location set + address field prefilled ONLY IF empty
    note right of SP
      A failed SEARCH (no results / 429 / network) never touches the pin -
      inline state only, never blocks submit.
    end note
  end
end
SP -> SHG : create(request)
SHG -> AC : post<ShelterDto>('/api/shelters', body)
AC -> API : POST /api/shelters
alt 201 Created + Location header
  API --> AC : ShelterDto (source=USER, status=ACTIVE)
  SP --> Person : navigate('/shelters/{id}')
else 400 out-of-Estonia/fields / 401 anonymous / 403 not verified / 409 cap or near-duplicate / 429 daily cap
  API --> AC : ErrorResponse
  SP --> Person : banner with message (input preserved; 403 adds a /verify link; 409 = "The limit of 10 active shelters has been reached")
end

note over DP
  USER-submitted rows are sacred on the backend: the registry
  importer never touches source=USER shelters.
end note

== Manage my contributions (M8, account page) ==
note over CP
  The /account page's "My contributions" panel (ContributionsPanel,
  embedded in AccountPage). It lists the caller's own shelters (the
  review half is gone with the review model); each row carries its
  reviewStatus (NEW / CONFIRMED / REJECTED), the admin's reviewNote and
  the moderator's infoRequest when present. Edits are inline-expanding
  forms (no modals); deletes are two-step confirms (no window.confirm).
end note
Person -> CP : open /account
== shelters list ==
CP -> SHG : mine()
SHG -> AC : get<MineShelterDto[]>('/api/shelters/mine')
AC -> API : GET /api/shelters/mine (Bearer JWT)
API --> CP : MineShelterDto[] (the caller's USER rows, ALL statuses)
note over CP
  Auto-hidden (INACTIVE) and REJECTED rows stay in the owner's list, each
  marked "Hidden - reported by the community (N reports)" (or the admin's
  REJECT reason) - no restore action (restore is admin-only).
end note
Person -> CP : edit a shelter row (inline form)
CP -> SHG : update(id, name/lat/lng/description/capacity)
SHG -> AC : put<ShelterDto>('/api/shelters/{id}', body)
alt 200 updated
  API --> CP : ShelterDto -> row updated in place (no page reload)
else 400 (bbox/fields) / 403 (not the author) / 404 (absent)
  API --> CP : ErrorResponse -> banner via bannerMessage, row unchanged
end
Person -> CP : delete a shelter (two-step confirm)
CP -> SHG : remove(id)
SHG -> AC : delete('/api/shelters/{id}')
AC -> API : DELETE /api/shelters/{id}
API --> CP : 204 No Content -> row removed (reports and occupancy cascade)
Person -> CP : answer the moderator's information request (one-time)
CP -> SHG : replyInfoRequest(id, message)
SHG -> AC : post<void>('/api/shelters/{id}/info-request/reply', {message})
AC -> API : POST /api/shelters/{id}/info-request/reply
alt 204 No Content
  API --> CP : row patched in place (the reply is read-only afterwards)
else 404 (no request) / 409 (already answered)
  API --> CP : ErrorResponse -> row error via bannerMessage
end
@enduml
